    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Zebra Technologies Corp is a public company headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois, and traded under the ticker ZBRA. Its SEC filing identifier is 0000877212. On its own site the company describes itself as powering intelligent operations, saying it helps organizations digitize, automate and enhance processes using mobile computers, scanners, printers and RFID, along with hardware and software for manufacturing automation, data analysis and factory connectivity.\n\nThe site presents a set of AI offerings aimed at frontline and industrial work. These include Zebra Companion AI, which the company describes as providing instant, tailored insights and support; Zebra Frontline AI Enablers, described as AI vision models, sample apps and APIs; and Zebra Frontline AI Blueprints, described as adaptable frameworks that automate manual tasks. The Zebra Aurora suite of machine vision software covers track-and-trace, vision inspection and industrial automation, and Zebra Aurora Focus is presented as a single interface for setting up, deploying and running the company's fixed industrial scanners and machine vision smart cameras. Zebra says its AI is an intelligent and open platform built to integrate with RFID, enterprise software and machine vision. The site also notes that some content or images may have been created with the assistance of AI, and that the Zebra wordmark and logo are trademarks of Zebra Technologies Corp., registered in many jurisdictions worldwide.\n\nLitigation exposure for the company is recorded in Illinois, with 375 cases.",
